
[1mBackup Commands[0m

Usage: tacctl backup <subcommand> [arguments]

Subcommands:
  list                                       Show snapshots, then old-style backups
  diff [<timestamp>]                         Diff store.yaml and tacctl.yaml against a snapshot (default: most recent)
  restore <timestamp> [--legacy|--keep-uids]  Restore a snapshot (with confirmation); --legacy for an old-style backup
      --legacy                               The timestamp names an old-style backup (backups/legacy)
      --keep-uids                            Leave the UID ledger (linux-uids) as it is; the registry, records and staging come back
  keep <timestamp> [--note <text>]           Copy a snapshot to backups-kept/, where no retention reaches it
      --note <text>                          Why it is kept (free text, shown by list, never logged)
  unkeep <timestamp> [--yes]                 Remove the kept copy of a snapshot (with confirmation)
      --yes                                  Do not ask for confirmation

